cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "NeuroVAT: a neuromorphic Verilog-A test bench and crossbar spiking-network simulator"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Peyal
    given-names: Md Mahmudul Kabir
    affiliation: Boise State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/mpeyal/neurovat-verilog-tester"
abstract: >-
  NeuroVAT is a test bench for neuromorphic synaptic device models. Its
  neurovat package simulates crossbar arrays of pluggable device models with
  leaky integrate-and-fire neurons, winner-take-all inhibition, device-local
  STDP and surrogate-gradient training, and runs seeded, config-driven sweeps
  of device variation, spike-time jitter and input noise.
keywords:
  - neuromorphic computing
  - spiking neural networks
  - STDP
  - ferroelectric devices
  - crossbar arrays
  - in-memory computing
